<title>UK: INTERVIEW-Rank says free to focus on core.</title>
<headline>INTERVIEW-Rank says free to focus on core.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rank Group Plc chief executive Andrew Teare said the leisure company could now get out of &quot;disposal mode&quot; after agreeing to sell its 20 percent stake in Rank Xerox to Xerox Corp.</p>
<p>&quot;I'm very pleased with the price and it (the deal) is earlier than we expected,&quot; Teare told Reuters in a telephone interview. &quot;A big piece of historic baggage has been dealt with,&quot; he added.</p>
<p>Xerox will pay up to one billion stg for the stake, with an inital 500 million stg to be paid on completion, expected by the end of this month.</p>
</text>
